        "original_id": "a04ecc4c-1111-5926-94f6-f1be4c71fcf0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Port Noarlunga Reef Aquatic Reserve, Gulf St Vincent, Adelaide metropolitan area, Onkaparinga River, Southern Adelaide, Adelaide, South Australia\n- Concepts: marine protected areas, rivers, Kaurna language\n\nFacts:\n- Port Noarlunga Reef Aquatic Reserve is a marine protected area in the Australian state of South Australia.\n- Port Noarlunga Reef Aquatic Reserve is located in waters in Gulf St Vincent adjoining the Adelaide metropolitan area.\n- Port Noarlunga Reef Aquatic Reserve includes part of the Onkaparinga River and lies about 28 km south-west of Adelaide.\n- The Onkaparinga River is known as Ngangkiparri in the Kaurna language.\n- The Onkaparinga River is a river in the Southern Adelaide region of South Australia.",
